    "Description": "The kernel packages contain the Linux kernel, the core of any Linux operating system.\n\nSecurity Fix(es):\n\n* kernel: xfrm: Duplicate SPI Handling (CVE-2025-39797)\n\n* kernel: Linux kernel: Denial of Service in qla2xxx SCSI driver due to improper command handling after chip reset (CVE-2025-68745)\n\n* kernel: Bluetooth: MGMT: validate LTK enc_size on load (CVE-2026-43020)\n\n* kernel: Bluetooth: SCO: fix race conditions in sco_sock_connect() (CVE-2026-43023)\n\n* kernel: netfilter: nfnetlink_cthelper: fix OOB read in nfnl_cthelper_dump_table() (CVE-2026-43450)\n\n* kernel: crypto: pcrypt - Fix handling of MAY_BACKLOG requests (CVE-2026-43493)\n\n* kernel: Linux kernel: xfrm single-frag length not properly limited ()\n\n* kernel: scsi: target: configfs: Bound snprintf() return in tg_pt_gp_members_show() (CVE-2026-46149)\n\n* kernel: procfs: fix missing RCU protection when reading real_parent in do_task_stat() (CVE-2026-46259)\n\n* kernel: crypto: af_alg - Cap AEAD AD length to 0x80000000 (CVE-2026-52972)\n\n* kernel: mac802154: llsec: add skb_cow_data() before in-place crypto (CVE-2026-63831)\n\n* kernel: blk-cgroup: fix UAF in __blkcg_rstat_flush() (CVE-2026-63802)\n\n* kernel: vxlan: do not reuse cached ip_hdr() value after skb_tunnel_check_pmtu() (CVE-2026-63993)\n\n* kernel: blk-mq: pop cached request if it is usable (CVE-2026-64017)\n\n* kernel: nvmet-auth: validate reply message payload bounds against transfer length (CVE-2026-64319)\n\n* kernel: selinux: check connect-related permissions on TCP Fast Open (CVE-2026-72243)\n\n* kernel: ALSA: usx2y: bound the hwdep mmap fault offset (CVE-2026-74641)\n\n* kernel: scsi: qla2xxx: Bound rsp_info_len to avoid OOB sense-data read (CVE-2026-89846)\n\n* kernel: kernel: strparser: use-after-free via msg_timer_work rearm after strp_done() cancellation ()\n\nBug Fix(es) and Enhancement(s):\n\n* kernel panics caused by NULL pointer dereferences within octeon_ep_vf [rhel-9.4.z] (JIRA:RHEL-186329)\n\n* BUG: sleeping function called from invalid context at kernel/locking/mutex.c:580 [rhel-9.4.z] (JIRA:RHEL-242406)\n\n* Kernel panic reboot node with kernal version 5.14.0-427.68.1.el9_4 [rhel-9.4.z] (JIRA:RHEL-273436)\n\nFor more details about the security issue(s), including the impact, a CVSS score, acknowledgments, and other related information, refer to the CVE page(s) listed in the References section.",
